# Source pins for the Python lint/format tools. This file lists only the
# top-level tools; the fully resolved, hash-pinned lock that pip actually
# installs is scripts/lint/requirements-lint.txt (generated from this file).
#
# Every tool is pinned to an exact version from PyPI, a trusted language
# package registry. Nothing here is fetched from GitHub Releases and no
# hook repository is git-cloned at commit time (issue #667).
#
# ruff tracks the version pinned for the ruff-pre-commit hook (issue #673).
# pre-commit-hooks provides the generic hygiene checks as console scripts
# (trailing-whitespace-fixer, end-of-file-fixer, check-yaml, check-toml,
# check-json, check-xml, check-merge-conflict, check-added-large-files,
# check-shebang-scripts-are-executable); it is the same
# pre-commit/pre-commit-hooks project, just installed from PyPI instead of
# cloned. scripts/lint/lint.sh is the authority on which are wired up and why
# some of the package's other checks are not. mdformat and its plugins format
# Markdown (issue #681).
#
# mdformat-gfm (not mdformat-tables) provides GFM pipe-table support;
# mdformat-tables is deprecated and its repo archived. See
# .claude/hooks/session-start.sh for the full rationale on the mdformat pins.
#
# Regenerating the lock (do this whenever a pin here changes):
#
#   uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.10 --generate-hashes \
#       scripts/lint/requirements-lint.in -o scripts/lint/requirements-lint.txt
#
# That command keeps the versions already present in the lock, so on its own it
# only re-resolves what a changed pin in this file forces. Transitive releases
# published since the last run are left alone, including security fixes for
# packages nothing here pins directly (issue #788). Add --upgrade to re-resolve
# the whole closure, or -P/--upgrade-package NAME to move one package and
# whatever it drags with it, which keeps a security bump to a reviewable diff.
#
# `uv` is not installed by the session-start hook. Install it first with
# `pip install uv` (see .claude/environment.md).
#
# --universal + --python-version 3.10 make the lock a superset that covers
# every interpreter the install sites use (system python3 in
# .claude/hooks/session-start.sh, and setup-python's "3.x" in CI), so
# marker-gated entries (for example tomli on Python < 3.11) resolve
# correctly wherever pip runs it under --require-hashes.
ruff==0.15.21
pre-commit-hooks==6.0.0
mdformat==1.0.0
mdformat-gfm==1.0.0
mdformat-frontmatter==2.1.2
